;; clojure-lsp, for the editor.
;;
;; The Problems panel is driven by clojure-lsp rather than by the `clj-kondo`
;; binary, and the two disagree about this repository for a structural reason:
;; it is not one project. It is forty-odd independent ones -- every lab and
;; every archived attempt has its own root, deps.edn and toolchain -- and a
;; namespace only resolves relative to the project that owns it.
;;
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Ignored trees
;;
;; Analysed as a single workspace, the archived projects produce findings that
;; are not true. `registry.server/build-router is called with 0 args but
;; expects 3` names a function that takes none; `Unresolved var: post-json`
;; names a var defined nine lines above its use. Lint the same files from
;; their own roots and both report zero errors and zero warnings.
;;
;; `.clj-kondo/config.edn` carries the matching `:output :exclude-files` for
;; the command line, and the two must agree or the editor and CI are back to
;; giving different answers -- which is the exact problem that file exists to
;; solve. `target.*` is clojure-lsp's own default and has to be repeated,
;; because setting this key replaces it rather than adding to it.
;;
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; unused-public-var, and why it is off
;;
;; This one is switched off knowing the findings were accurate. They were
;; checked: `lab29.payments.api/dead-letters` really has no caller, and so do
;; another fifty-odd vars across labs 15 to 29.
;;
;; What is wrong is the linter's premise, not its analysis. It assumes an
;; unreferenced public var is dead code to delete. In a teaching repository it
;; usually is not. Lab 29 gives Catalog, Ordering and Payments the same
;; nine-function API -- `dead-letters`, `revive!`, `audit-log` and the rest --
;; *because the symmetry is the lesson*, and the suite happens to exercise
;; dead-lettering through Catalog only. Deleting Payments' copy to satisfy the
;; linter would damage the thing the lab is demonstrating.
;;
;; The cost of leaving it on is worse than the noise it reports: fifty-nine
;; permanent entries train a reader to ignore the panel, and the next real
;; finding arrives into a list nobody looks at. clj-kondo still runs over every
;; lab, and `bb lint` in each lab is still zero errors and zero warnings.
;;
;; If you want the report anyway, it is one command and no configuration:
;;
;;     clojure-lsp diagnostics
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{:source-paths-ignore-regex ["target.*"
                             "archive.*"
                             ".*\\.clj-kondo/imports.*"
                             ".*\\.clj-kondo/\\.cache.*"
                             ".*\\.lsp/\\.cache.*"]

 :linters {:clojure-lsp/unused-public-var {:level :off}}}
